## ✅ **SSC CGL 2025 Exam Pattern Overview**

SSC CGL परीक्षा में कुल **2 चरण (Tiers)** होते हैं:

| Tier   | Mode         | Type of Exam    |
| ------ | ------------ | --------------- |
| Tier 1 | Online (CBT) | Objective (MCQ) |
| Tier 2 | Online (CBT) | Objective (MCQ) |

---

## 🧪 **Tier-I Exam Pattern (Prelims)**

| Subject                          | Questions | Marks   | Time           |
| -------------------------------- | --------- | ------- | -------------- |
| General Intelligence & Reasoning | 25        | 50      |                |
| General Awareness                | 25        | 50      |                |
| Quantitative Aptitude            | 25        | 50      |                |
| English Comprehension            | 25        | 50      |                |
| **Total**                        | **100**   | **200** | **60 Minutes** |

### 🔹 Important Points:

* Negative Marking: **0.50 marks** for each wrong answer.
* Qualifying in nature – Final selection नहीं तय करता।

---

## 🧮 **Tier-II Exam Pattern (Mains)**

Tier II में अब सिर्फ **3 Papers** होते हैं:

### 📘 **Paper-I (Compulsory for all posts)**

| Module          | Sections                           | Marks      | Time    |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------- | ---------- | ------- |
| **Section-I**   | Mathematical Abilities + Reasoning | 60 + 30 Qs | 90 mins |
| **Section-II**  | English Language & Comprehension   | 45 Qs      | –       |
| **Section-III** | Data Entry Speed Test (DEST)       | Qualifying | –       |

### 📘 **Paper-II**:

* **For Junior Statistical Officer (JSO)**
* Subject: Statistics
* Questions: 100 | Marks: 200 | Time: 2 Hours

### 📘 **Paper-III**:

* **For Assistant Audit Officer/Assistant Accounts Officer (AAO)**
* Subject: General Studies (Finance & Economics)
* Questions: 100 | Marks: 200 | Time: 2 Hours

---

## 📚 **SSC CGL Tier Wise Detailed Syllabus**

---

### 🔹 **Tier-I Syllabus**

#### 1. **General Intelligence & Reasoning**:

* Analogy, Classification, Series
* Coding-Decoding, Puzzle
* Venn Diagram, Syllogism
* Blood Relation, Direction
* Missing Number, Clock & Calendar

#### 2. **General Awareness**:

* Static GK (History, Polity, Geography, Economy, Science)
* Current Affairs (Last 6–8 months)
* Books & Authors, Important Days
* Awards, Sports, Government Schemes

#### 3. **Quantitative Aptitude**:

* Number System, HCF & LCM
* Ratio, Percentage, Profit & Loss
* SI & CI, Time & Work, Time & Distance
* Mensuration, Algebra, Geometry
* Trigonometry, Data Interpretation

#### 4. **English Language**:

* Vocabulary (Synonyms/Antonyms)
* Grammar (Tenses, Articles, Prepositions)
* Cloze Test, Sentence Improvement
* Comprehension, Error Spotting

---

### 🔹 **Tier-II Syllabus (Main Topics)**

#### 🔸 **Mathematical Abilities**:

* Advanced Math: Algebra, Trigonometry, Geometry, Mensuration
* Arithmetic: Percentage, Profit & Loss, Ratio, SI/CI, Time & Work, Boats & Streams

#### 🔸 **Reasoning**:

* Verbal and Non-Verbal Reasoning
* Coding-Decoding, Analogies, Series
* Data Sufficiency, Decision Making

#### 🔸 **English Language**:

* Grammar, Usage, Spotting Error
* Reading Comprehension
* Sentence Improvement
* Para Jumbles, Active-Passive, Narration

#### 🔸 **Statistics (JSO post)**:

* Collection & Classification of Data
* Measures of Central Tendency
* Correlation & Regression
* Probability Theory, Time Series

#### 🔸 **General Studies (Finance & Economics - AAO post)**:

* Indian Economy
* Finance Commission Role
* Budget, Inflation, Banking
* Basic Economic Concepts

---

## 📝 **Final Selection Criteria:**

* Based on **Tier II only** (Tier I is qualifying).
* For some posts like Tax Assistant, Computer Proficiency Test/Data Entry Skill Test is also required.

